    "body": "## Motivation\n\nOLMoE can't run with `--tp-size > 1` on any platform (#11651, which was auto-closed and is still reproducible on current `main`). `OlmoeAttention` applies `q_norm` / `k_norm`, which are RMSNorms over **all** heads (`hidden_size`), directly to the per-rank q/k shards. The first forward fails:\n\n```\nFile \".../models/olmoe.py\", line 191, in forward\nValueError: Expected hidden_size to be 2048, but found: 1024\n```\n\nComments on #11651 report the same failure on NVIDIA (A100, TP=2, in a FlashInfer RMSNorm shape check). I hit it on AMD Radeon while validating TP2 there.\n\n## Modifications\n\nSame approach as `olmo2.py`'s `_apply_qk_norm` (and vLLM's OLMoE):\n\n- When `tp_size > 1`, all-gather q and k across the TP group, apply the full-width norms, then take this rank's slice back with `split_tensor_along_last_dim`.\n- `k_norm` is sized `total_num_kv_heads * head_dim` instead of `hidden_size`. They are equal for OLMoE checkpoints (16 KV heads), so nothing changes there, but the norm now matches k's width.\n\nTP=1 does exactly the same arithmetic as before.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nallenai/OLMoE-1B-7B-0125-Instruct on RDNA4 (gfx1201 ×2, PCIe):\n\n- Stock `rocm/pytorch` image.\n- `main` + #43679 + #47254 (needed for this GPU) + a local quark-import guard.\n- Default server flags (Triton attention, decode CUDA graphs).\n- gsm8k: `sgl-eval==0.1.2`, 200 questions, temperature 0.7, top_p 0.8.\n- Throughput: `bench_serving` random-ids 512/256.\n\n| | without this PR, TP2 | with this PR, TP2 | with this PR, TP1 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| server | ❌ `ValueError: Expected hidden_size to be 2048, but found: 1024` | ✅ | ✅ |\n| gsm8k (200) | — | 59.0% | 60.5% |\n| c=1 output tok/s (median TPOT) | — | 122.8 (8.0 ms) | 97.8 (10.1 ms) |\n| c=8 output tok/s (median TPOT) | — | 623.4 (12.3 ms) | 446.4 (17.5 ms) |\n\nTP2 matches TP1 accuracy within sampling noise.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nSee above. The extra all-gather is two small `[tokens, hidden]` tensors per layer, as in OLMo2.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (Needs a multi-GPU OLMoE run; validated end to end above.)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No doc change needed.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results. (See above.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40879075578](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40879075578)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40879075450](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40879075450)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40879075540](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40879075540)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
